# LEGAL DOCUMENTS -- deliberately not formatted.
#
# public/legal holds the agent, company and investment agreements, the privacy
# policy, the risk disclosure and the terms of service, in four languages: 24
# files. A formatting pass is a code-style change and these are not code.
#
# Whitespace between inline elements in HTML is SIGNIFICANT -- it collapses to a
# single space rather than to nothing -- so reflowing them can move text on a
# rendered page, and the diff would be large, unreviewable and across documents
# that carry legal weight. Excluded on 2026-08-25, when a formatting pass first
# reached them: 187 files needed formatting and 24 were these.
public/legal

# GENERATED FROM THE BACKEND'S OpenAPI SCHEMA -- formatting it is a treadmill.
#
# The production box regenerates src/api/generated.ts during `aivis update` and
# PUSHES the result itself, on a cadence this repo does not control: measured
# 2026-08-25, thirty-two such commits exist in history (git log --all --grep
# "regenerate generated" -- frontend/src/api/generated.ts). Q4 formatted the file
# on 2026-08-25 and the very next deploy (6bf9090) undid it, took `npm run lint`
# from exit 0 to exit 1, and rotted a live citation by shifting a line.
#
# Any formatting applied here is guaranteed to be reverted by a machine, so this
# is not a style exemption -- it is declining to fight a generator.
#
# NOT A NEW EXCEPTION: eslint.config.js already carries a per-file rule override
# for this exact path, with its reason at lines 27-30. This brings prettier into
# line with a decision eslint already holds.
src/api/generated.ts
